// golden_test.go — T-47: the generated-golden differential for the
// vaultseal module — slugify, describe()/to_dict(), the message doors
// (the frozen clock), the owner door (the 401 hint), the creation
// guard's exact errors + the POST body, the managed .gitignore blocks
// (merge/rebuild/coexistence + the CRLF tail quirk), the belt's
// untrack law (files stay on disk) + the _review twin, the resync
// delta counts, the fnmatch table, status() (deterministic shas), the
// bridge belt join, and the FETCH_HEAD scrub.
//
// testdata/vaultseal.golden.json is generated by
// testdiff/goldens/dump_vaultseal.py from the unmodified reference
// (assadigit/GitCurator @ 98f4fc7, the pinned venv's CPython 3.12.15
// stdlib) — no per-run facts inside: every temp-vault path is folded
// to '<vault>/…', the CLOCK is frozen (the message doors), and the
// GIT DATES are frozen (deterministic commit shas).
//
// THE LAW: goldens are never hand-edited; a divergence is either a Go
// bug (fix the port) or a reference behavior change (regenerate + say
// so in the commit).
package vaultseal

